      q: `<p>Alex asks Sophia several times to change how his project is managed, believing it will make the project much more successful. Sophia refuses and tells him to do it her way. Rewrite Sophia's response using collaborating, and explain what she gains and what it costs.</p>`,
      options: null, correct: null,
      answer: `<p><b>Model answer.</b> Rewritten response: "Alex, you've raised this several times, so let's sit down properly. Walk me through the changes and why you think they'll work. I also need the project to stay within budget and on schedule. Let's see which of your changes meet both, and try them for the next phase." This is collaborating: Sophia states her own concerns (budget, schedule) and works to satisfy Alex's (a better-run project). <b>Gains</b>: Alex feels heard instead of upset; she may improve the project, the opportunity the course says she missed; she is seen as a skilled manager; Alex is committed to the solution. <b>Costs</b>: time, a meeting and perhaps a trial period, and some delay while the changes are tested.</p>`,
