      options: null, correct: null,
      answer: `<p><b>Model answer.</b> (a) <b>Accommodating</b>: the issue is small, I care less than the others and prolonging it isn't worth the time; letting them choose keeps the peace. (b) <b>Competing</b>: a quick decision, such as choosing the venue myself, stops a small conflict escalating or wasting time. The notes call this kind of use appropriate in Sophia's escape-room decision. (c) <b>Collaborating</b>: the labs must work together for years and the booking system has a significant impact on both, so it is worth sitting down to understand each lab's needs (peak times, long experiments) and design a schedule that meets both.</p>`,
