      options: null, correct: null,
      answer: `<p><b>Model answer.</b> The case is set in Room No. 10, the CMO's office in district Badgam, on the day of the monthly meeting. Mr Kumar, a BEE from one PHC, has a prior appointment with the CMO's PA. Dr Kapoor, a BMO from another PHC, is chatting with the PA, so Kumar waits outside. As the meeting time nears, Kumar goes in and reminds the PA of his appointment. Kapoor, irritated, shouts at him to leave and calls him an idiot. Kumar leaves crestfallen with tears in his eyes and tells the BEEs, Supervisors and LHVs in the corridor, who take it as an insult to the whole group. The Dy. CMOs, MOs and specialists gather and advise him to forget about it and seek a fresh appointment. Shouts, abuses, heated arguments and some physical attacks follow, and a medical group and a paramedical group form. The paramedical group tells the CMO that he always harasses, discriminates against and suppresses them. Kumar's group asks for a written apology, Kapoor's group refuses, and the CMO decides to arrange a direct confrontation meeting between the two groups.</p>`,
